                "To consolidate the technical architecture, General IT Control evaluations, assertion-level risk mappings, and business model risk decompositions mastered across Day 31, audit data engineers and senior assurance partners construct an end-to-end Algorithmic Inherent Risk Scoring and Financial Statement Level RoMM Simulator. This enterprise simulator models a Big Four audit engagement team planning the statutory audit of a multi-billion-dollar diversified industrial conglomerate, automating the synthesis of qualitative inherent risk factors and quantitative operational metrics into an audited risk assessment model under ISA 315 (Revised 2019) and PCAOB AS 2110. In contemporary global assurance practice, reliance on subjective gut feelings or legacy spreadsheet templates is no longer acceptable to audit inspection regulators. By formalizing audit risk logic into programmatic algorithms, audit teams achieve repeatable, objective, and mathematically defensible risk judgments.",
